1.  **`timeoutId` Variable:**
    *   We declare a variable outside the returned function (in the closure scope). This variable stores the ID returned by `setTimeout`. It persists across multiple calls to the debounced function.

2.  **Returned Function (`return function(...args) { ... }`):**
    *   This is the function that the user will actually call (e.g., `debouncedSearch('some text')`).
    *   **`const context = this;`**: We capture the `this` context of the call. This is crucial so that when the original function runs, it executes with the correct `this` (e.g., if it was a method on an object).
    *   **`if (timeoutId) { clearTimeout(timeoutId); }`**: This is the core of debouncing. Every time the debounced function is called, we immediately cancel any previously scheduled execution. This prevents older, pending calls from running.
